# Domain rules and wiring

## Status vs progress vs complete

| Field | Where | Who writes |
|---|---|---|
| `Task.status` | `todo`, `in_progress`, `done` | Admin: any. Lead: `todo` or `in_progress` only. Complete is `POST /tasks/{id}/complete`. |
| `TaskAssignment.progress` | 0–100 | Lead (or admin) via `PATCH /tasks/{id}/assignments/{user_id}`. |
| `TaskAssignment.rating` | 1–5 optional | Same PATCH. |

Dashboard percent = average of assignment progress on the project; `done` tasks count as 100.

Lead **cannot** PATCH status to `done`. After saving progress, UI asks to mark completed → `POST /complete`.

## Membership vs assignment

- `ProjectMember` — user is on the project. Leads see the project; assignees must be members.
- `TaskAssignment` — user is on the task. Creates notification. Shown on My tasks.

Don't assign someone who isn't a project member (service should reject).

## Notifications

Created when a task assignment **adds** a user. Member uses the bell + My tasks. Marking read is `PATCH /notifications/{id}/read` or read-all.

## Frontend → API (who calls what)

All calls go through `apps/frontend/src/api/index.ts` + `client.ts` (Bearer token).

| UI | API |
|---|---|
| Login | `POST /api/users/login` (`application/x-www-form-urlencoded` `username`, `password`) |
| Register | `POST /api/users/register` |
| Admin users | `/api/users/` CRUD |
| Admin/lead projects | `/api/projects/` ; members `PUT /{id}/members` |
| Dashboard | `GET /api/projects/{id}/dashboard` |
| Create/edit task | `POST/PATCH /api/tasks/` |
| Assign | `POST /api/tasks/{id}/assign` `{ user_ids }` |
| Lead progress | `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/assignments/{user_id}` |
| Lead complete | `POST /api/tasks/{id}/complete` |
| My tasks | `GET /api/users/me/tasks` |
| Task detail | `GET /api/tasks/{id}` |
| Generate description | `POST /api/ai/generate-task` `{ title }` |
| Notifications | `GET /api/notifications/` |

## Auth header
`Authorization: Bearer <token>` from `localStorage` `taskmanager_token`. 401 → send user to login.

## Don't
- Don't add a fourth role.
- Don't let members PATCH tasks or assignments.
- Don't compute dashboard % in the React app if the backend already returns it.
- Don't call NVIDIA from the frontend.
- Don't skip notifications when adding assignees.
